Role of OLAP
OLAP (Online Analytical Processing) supports multidimensional analysis: student marks (the
measure) can be viewed along several dimensions at the same time, such as department, city and time
(semester).
 - Roll-up: summarise to a higher level (city-wise averages to state-wise, or department averages to
   college average).
 - Drill-down: go from totals to detail (from college average down to department, then to a single
   student).
 - Slice and dice: pick one value or a sub-cube of the data (only the IT department (slice), or IT and
   CS students from Pune and Mumbai (dice)).
 - Pivot: rotate the view to compare two dimensions side by side.
 - OLAP gives fast answers on large historical data, so decision makers can see trends without
   writing complex queries.
Conclusion: simple SQL (SELECT, aggregate functions, GROUP BY) gives the required reports,
and OLAP lets us analyse the same data from many angles.


