Output:
  { patient_name: 'Karan Singh', age: 70 }
  { patient_name: 'Amit Joshi', age: 60 }
  { patient_name: 'Rahul Desai', age: 52 }

Query 8: $regex: patient names starting with R
  db.patients.find(
    { patient_name: { $regex: '^R' } },
    { _id: 0, patient_name: 1 }
  )

Output:
  { patient_name: 'Ravi Patil' }
  { patient_name: 'Rahul Desai' }

Query 9: Nested field: patients living in Pune
  db.patients.find(
    { 'contact.city': 'Pune' },
    { _id: 0, patient_name: 1, contact: 1 }
  )

Output:
  { patient_name: 'Ravi Patil', contact: { phone: '9876500001', city: 'Pune' } }
  { patient_name: 'Sneha Rao', contact: { phone: '9876500004', city: 'Pune' } }
  { patient_name: 'Neha More', contact: { phone: '9876500006', city: 'Pune' } }

Query 10: sort by name with skip() and limit() (pagination)
  db.patients.find({}, { _id: 0, patient_name: 1, department: 1 })
    .sort({ patient_name: 1 })
    .skip(2).limit(3)

Output:
  { patient_name: 'Neha More', department: 'Pediatrics' }
  { patient_name: 'Priya Shah', department: 'Neurology' }
  { patient_name: 'Rahul Desai', department: 'Neurology' }

Query 11: distinct(): list of departments
  db.patients.distinct('department')

Output:
  ['Cardiology', 'Neurology', 'Orthopedics', 'Pediatrics']

Query 12: Aggregation $group: patients and average age per department
  db.patients.aggregate([
    { $group: { _id: '$department',
                patients: { $sum: 1 },
                avgAge: { $avg: '$age' } } },
    { $sort: { _id: 1 } }
  ])

Output:
  { _id: 'Cardiology', patients: 3, avgAge: 58.333333333333336 }
  { _id: 'Neurology', patients: 2, avgAge: 42.0 }
  { _id: 'Orthopedics', patients: 1, avgAge: 28.0 }
  { _id: 'Pediatrics', patients: 1, avgAge: 19.0 }

Conclusion: comparison, logical, regex, nested-field, sort/skip/limit, distinct and aggregation
operators allow patients to be retrieved, filtered and sorted in many ways.
